doi_def->map.std->lvl.local = kcalloc(doi_def->map.std->lvl.local_size, sizeof(u32), GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NOWARN);
doi_def->map.std->lvl.cipso = kcalloc(doi_def->map.std->lvl.cipso_size, sizeof(u32), GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NOWARN);
```
Reason:
The addition of the `__GFP_NOWARN` flag to the `kcalloc()` calls suppresses the warnings that occur when the allocation size is deemed too large. This allows the allocation to proceed without unnecessary warnings, acknowledging that the size values come from user input and may not always be indicative of a programming error.

